{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1173211-interesting-article-about-fear","id":1173211,"title":"Interesting article about fear","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-04T07:32:31-08:00","id":1173211,"title":"Interesting article about fear","content":"I saw this article, and I thought that it might be of interest to my fellow Beast fans: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/feeling-too-much/201409/the-reverberations-fear\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn2.psychologytoday.com/assets/styles/manual_crop_1_91_1_1528x800/public/blogs/77234/2014/09/160129-164533_0.jpg?itok=Is2oBaKc\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/feeling-too-much/201409/the-reverberations-fear\" target=\"_blank\"> The Reverberations of Fear </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/feeling-too-much/201409/the-reverberations-fear\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/feeling-too-much/201409/the-reverberations-fear </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Extreme fear registers not just in the individual but can actually make his or her children - and his or her children's children - more sensitive to the same fearful stimuli. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:38:26-08:00","id":1173245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1173211-interesting-article-about-fear#post1173211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this article, and I thought that it might be of interest to my fellow Beast fans:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/feeling-too-much/201409/the-reverberations-fear\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog...berations-fear</a></div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, the forum is not letting me put a like (says I'm not logged in while it's evident I am), so I guess I'll reply directly.<br /> <br /> It was a very interesting read and something worth remembering, thanks for sharing it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T11:01:42-08:00","id":1173264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1173211-interesting-article-about-fear?p=1173245#post1173245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, the forum is not letting me put a like (says I'm not logged in while it's evident I am), so I guess I'll reply directly.<br /> <br /> It was a very interesting read and something worth remembering, thanks for sharing it</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. I'm confident that I'll eventually come up with a good way to put this to use in a game, even if I haven't figured it out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T06:20:30-08:00","id":1173476,"title":"","content":"It makes me wonder what other alterations happen epigenetically generation to generation, and what we could do with gene therapies etc...<br /> <br /> And you know, what would happen to implement this as a long-standing beast who has effectively dominated an area, reinforcing his nightmare over generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T08:37:07-08:00","id":1173492,"title":"","content":"Cool article! And very interesting hypothesis. Kinda Lamarck, but not as extreme.<br /> <br /> And it kinda makes sense in the context of the ChroD. Learn to fear all those things that go bump in the night, respond by pretending they don't exist -&gt; descendants do the same.<br /> In regards to Beast, wouldn't that make a long-standing Begotten especially effective in his claimed area? After all, people should more easily be scared by his nightmare, causing a Breaking Point more easily, which in turn should feed the Horror more effectively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T20:22:39-08:00","id":1173677,"title":"","content":"Mechanically it seems like the kind of thing you'd model with a Condition, right? Something like this?<br /> <br /> <b>In the Blood</b><br /> Your family has long lived in the shadow of a particular Begotten, and the fear they cause has been passed down in your DNA. Any roll to resist the specified Beast's supernatural actions is made with a -3 die pool penalty.<br /> <br /> <i>Take a Beat: </i>when you fail a roll against the specified Beast.<br /> <br /> <i>Resolution: </i>Kill the specified Beast.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T02:55:28-08:00","id":1173721,"title":"","content":"Oh, I like the penalty to resisting that Beast's supernatural actions!<br /> <br /> Although I feel like it should be harder to resolve - killing The King of Spiders wouldn't mean I stop being afraid of icky spiders, after all. Then again, this IS supernatural in nature, so... maybe going face to face with it and coming out ahead causes a mindset that goes &quot;Pff, that spider is downright <i>cute</i>! I've killed way worse!&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:51:52-08:00","id":1173768,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more of the world building and setting effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:57:51-08:00","id":1173769,"title":"","content":"I figure this would be something many Incarnates would have a try with, in all fairness. Even more so if they're Apex<br /> <br /> EDIT: (Apexes is the correct term? Sorry, I'm really sick and my brain is refusing to work with non-native languages)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo